    "lossyReason": "PLAN.md S.10.2: psdexport emits layer channels in its own fixed order (0,1,2,-1; gray 0,-1) and always emits an alpha channel, because the engine model is RGBA. This fixture was authored with alpha first (-1,0,1,2) or with no alpha channel at all, so every re-exported record's channelIds differ in order and the flattened records gain a -1. The PSD spec does not prescribe channel order and readers key on the ID, so this is a spelling difference rather than lost data: the set of IDs is otherwise unchanged, the -2 user mask channel included. psd-tools 1.19.0 and ImageMagick 6.9.12-98 both read the re-export correctly. PLAN.md S.10.4: psdRecords[1].mask.rect - psdimport rasterizes the layer mask into a document-sized buffer and discards the mask rectangle, so the re-export stores a full-canvas mask rect instead of the original (10,7) 12x8. The mask still attenuates the layer; only its stored extent is widened.",
